- "intent": one of "move", "talk", "look", "interact", "examine", "unknown"
- "target": what the action is directed at (string or null)
- "dialogue": what the player is saying, if talking (string or null)

IMPORTANT: "move" is ONLY for when the player expresses a present desire to navigate somewhere (imperative or future intent). Narrative, past-tense, or reflective statements that merely mention a place name are "talk", not "move".

IMPORTANT: "look" is ONLY for a bare imperative observation command — "look", "look around", "examine the room", "where am I". A sentence that merely contains the word "look" inside conversational speech (e.g. "Might I look about the village a while?", "I'll have a look at the cattle later", "It looks fine to me") is "talk", not "look".

Examples:
Input: "go to the pub" → {"intent": "move", "target": "the pub", "dialogue": null}
Input: "talk to Mary" → {"intent": "talk", "target": "Mary", "dialogue": null}
Input: "tell Padraig I saw his cow" → {"intent": "talk", "target": "Padraig", "dialogue": "I saw his cow"}
Input: "look around" → {"intent": "look", "target": null, "dialogue": null}
Input: "Might I look about the village a while?" → {"intent": "talk", "target": null, "dialogue": "Might I look about the village a while?"}
Input: "I'll have a look at the cattle later" → {"intent": "talk", "target": null, "dialogue": "I'll have a look at the cattle later"}
Input: "pick up the stone" → {"intent": "interact", "target": "the stone", "dialogue": null}
Input: "tie a strip of cloth to the thorn bush" → {"intent": "interact", "target": "the thorn bush", "dialogue": null}
Input: "light the candle on the altar" → {"intent": "interact", "target": "the candle", "dialogue": null}
Input: "pour water into the basin" → {"intent": "interact", "target": "the basin", "dialogue": null}
Input: "kneel before the cross" → {"intent": "interact", "target": "the cross", "dialogue": null}
Input: "I came from the coast" → {"intent": "talk", "target": null, "dialogue": "I came from the coast"}
Input: "I was at the shore yesterday" → {"intent": "talk", "target": null, "dialogue": "I was at the shore yesterday"}

IMPORTANT: "interact" is for any imperative physical-action command — picking up, putting down, tying, lighting, pouring, filling, lifting, pumping, digging, placing, or touching/using an object. Do NOT classify physical-action imperatives as "talk".

